1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,820
Gloss has two front ends.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,020
The app, and the page.

3
00:00:05,680 --> 00:00:07,420
Both show the same code.

4
00:00:07,620 --> 00:00:12,580
If each one decided for itself which types lead a module, or what a map draws,

5
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:13,920
they would drift apart.

6
00:00:14,670 --> 00:00:16,730
So Gloss Map decides once.

7
00:00:17,030 --> 00:00:21,230
It arranges the model for reading, and both front ends draw from it.

8
00:00:23,233 --> 00:00:25,713
The Atlas is where the model and the lint meet.

9
00:00:26,463 --> 00:00:31,443
It takes each contract, which is a declaration as read, and pairs it with the lint's

10
00:00:31,443 --> 00:00:32,203
assessment of it.

11
00:00:32,603 --> 00:00:35,083
That pair is called a reviewed contract.

12
00:00:35,603 --> 00:00:36,883
The lint is optional.

13
00:00:37,203 --> 00:00:41,443
Without it, the contracts read the same, and there are simply no findings.

14
00:00:42,193 --> 00:00:45,093
From there the Atlas answers what a view asks.

15
00:00:45,293 --> 00:00:46,433
The levels of the map.

16
00:00:46,633 --> 00:00:47,273
The focus.

17
00:00:47,653 --> 00:00:48,733
What a type reaches.

18
00:00:49,073 --> 00:00:50,653
And why one type uses another.

19
00:00:52,667 --> 00:00:56,387
A big codebase can't be drawn as one graph a reader can follow.

20
00:00:56,747 --> 00:00:58,267
So the map has levels.

21
00:00:58,867 --> 00:01:03,607
It opens at the most detailed level that fits the budget, which is thirty boxes.

22
00:01:04,127 --> 00:01:05,887
Every type, if they fit.

23
00:01:06,447 --> 00:01:10,687
Otherwise each module as one box, and a reader steps into a module.

24
00:01:11,127 --> 00:01:14,207
A module too large for the budget is drawn as folders.

25
00:01:14,957 --> 00:01:19,977
What a level leaves outside is drawn as boundary boxes a reader can step into.

26
00:01:20,727 --> 00:01:23,847
Graph Layout places the boxes in rows, top to bottom.

27
00:01:24,167 --> 00:01:28,967
It runs once, in Swift, so the page draws fixed pictures and the app draws the

28
00:01:28,967 --> 00:01:29,547
same boxes.

29
00:01:29,907 --> 00:01:32,367
The same graph always gives the same drawing.

30
00:01:34,367 --> 00:01:37,787
For a change, Gloss Map finds what the change reaches.

31
00:01:38,347 --> 00:01:42,567
That is the blast radius, drawn from the types that changed, outward.

32
00:01:43,317 --> 00:01:47,517
A reach can follow what a type depends on, what uses it,

33
00:01:47,697 --> 00:01:48,437
or both.

34
00:01:49,017 --> 00:01:51,717
For each type reached, the map can say why.

35
00:01:51,997 --> 00:01:54,937
Why the thing it relies on changed, from the branch's story.

36
00:01:55,157 --> 00:01:57,677
And why it relies on that thing, from the docs.

37
00:01:58,427 --> 00:02:00,247
Findings are judged the same way.

38
00:02:01,027 --> 00:02:05,867
Changed Findings keeps only the findings on declarations the change added or changed.

39
00:02:06,347 --> 00:02:09,067
Code nobody touched can't fail the change.

40
00:02:09,817 --> 00:02:11,617
Gloss Map decides what to show.

41
00:02:11,937 --> 00:02:13,917
The app and the page just draw it.
